      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {
        "en": "Talking about music"
      },
      "texto": {
        "en": "People: **el cantante**, **el compositor**, **el músico**, **el guitarrista**, **el pianista**, **el director de orquesta**, **el bailarín**. Words in **-ista** keep the same ending in the masculine and feminine: **el / la** guitarrista.\n\nYou **tocas** an instrument: la guitarra, el piano, el violín, **la batería**. You **cantas**, **bailas**, **compones** and **ensayas**.\n\nA band **saca** un disco, **da** un concierto and **está de gira**. Music played or heard at a concert is **en directo** (or **en vivo**).\n\nA song has **letra** and **música**. A song that becomes very popular is **un éxito**.\n\nTo say what music does to you, use the **gustar** pattern: **me emociona**, **me relaja**, **me pone** de buen humor, **me recuerda a** mi infancia.\n\n**Tener buen oído** is to have a good ear. **Saberse** una canción **de memoria** is to know it by heart."
      }
    },
